# Rust Standards (ATSC v2)

## Error Handling

```rust
// BAD — never in non-test code
let val = something.unwrap();
let val = something.expect("msg");
panic!("something went wrong");

// GOOD — propagate with ?
let val = something?;

// GOOD — return descriptive error
return Err(Error::UnexpectedEof { offset, expected: 4 });
```

## Wire Format

- All integers: little-endian (`to_le_bytes()` / `from_le_bytes()`)
- No `usize` in encode/decode — only `u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `i64`
- Bounds-check every read before indexing:

```rust
// BAD
let val = u32::from_le_bytes(buf[off..off+4].try_into().unwrap());

// GOOD
if buf.len() < off + 4 {
    return Err(Error::UnexpectedEof { offset: off, expected: 4 });
}
let val = u32::from_le_bytes(buf[off..off+4].try_into().map_err(|_| {
    Error::UnexpectedEof { offset: off, expected: 4 }
})?);
```

## Public API

- Every `pub fn` has a doc comment with `# Errors` section
- `#[must_use]` on Result-returning functions
- Prefer `&[T]` over `Vec<T>` in parameters

## Testing

- Roundtrip test for every codec
- Corrupt-input test for every decode path
- No test should depend on external files — use inline constants
